[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // M5 -- overflow: glibc converts at `long` width, saturating at LONG_MAX /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // LONG_MIN, then truncates to `int`. These inputs pin that behaviour down.
