[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m      A version that saturated at `INT_MAX` would instead run ~2^31 iterations.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * `-99999999999999999999999 7` → `LONG_MIN` → `(int)` = `0`, `y = 7`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `Scanner::scan_i32` reproduces this with a checked `i64` accumulator that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    saturates to `i64::MIN`/`i64::MAX` and then narrows with `as i32`. Verified:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `values_above_int_range_are_truncated_to_int`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `values_beyond_long_range_saturate_then_truncate`, `fuzz_long_digit_runs`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. **`goto` semantics inside the `while` body.** `label1` and `label2` are both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    inside the loop body, so:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * `goto label2` (only when `x == 1 && y == 4`) skips the `label1` block *for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m      that entry only*;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * `goto label1` re-enters the body **without re-testing `x > 0 || y > 0`**,
